IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap2-3val`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2015(o): the work requirement for some adults (snap2).
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt, a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text; nothing here is verified against it.
-- JUST TRUE: the text says yes. JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words. NOTHING: the text does not say.
-- Percentages are fractions (15 percent is 0.15). Fiscal years are numbers (the 2027 fiscal year is 2027).

§ `Section 2015(o)(1): work program`

DECLARE `s 2015(o)(1) kind of program` IS ONE OF
    `s 2015(o)(1)(A) a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act`
    `s 2015(o)(1)(B) a program under section 2296 of title 19`
    `s 2015(o)(1)(C) a program of employment and training operated or supervised by a State or political subdivision` HAS
        `it meets standards approved by the Governor of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
        `it is a supervised job search program or a job search training program` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 2015(o)(1)(D) a program of employment and training for veterans operated by the Department of Labor or the Department of Veterans Affairs` HAS
        `it is approved by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 2015(o)(1)(E) a workforce partnership under subsection (d)(4)(N)`
    `s 2015(o)(1) another kind of program`

-- src:781 | In this subsection, the term “work program” means—
-- src:782 | (A) a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act [29 U.S.C. 3111 et seq.];
-- src:783 | (B) a program under section 2296 of title 19;
-- src:784 | (C) a program of employment and training operated or supervised by a State or political subdivision of a State that meets standards approved by the Governor of the State, including a program under subsection (d)(4), other than a supervised job search program or job search training program;
-- src:785 | (D) a program of employment and training for veterans operated by the Department of Labor or the Department of Veterans Affairs, and approved by the Secretary; and
-- src:786 | (E) a workforce partnership under subsection (d)(4)(N).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(1) (src:781-786)
GIVEN k IS A `s 2015(o)(1) kind of program`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(1) the program is a work program` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the term “work program” means— (A) ...; (B) ...; (C) ... other than a supervised job search program or job search training program; (D) ... approved by the Secretary; and (E) ..."
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `s 2015(o)(1)(A) a program under title I of the Workforce Innovation and Opportunity Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(o)(1)(B) a program under section 2296 of title 19` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- fork F-o1: "including a program under subsection (d)(4)" is read as an instance of the class, so a (d)(4) program also needs the Governor-approved standards; the other reading would count it without them
    WHEN `s 2015(o)(1)(C) a program of employment and training operated or supervised by a State or political subdivision` governor jobSearch THEN JUST (governor AND (NOT jobSearch))
    WHEN `s 2015(o)(1)(D) a program of employment and training for veterans operated by the Department of Labor or the Department of Veterans Affairs` approved THEN JUST approved
    WHEN `s 2015(o)(1)(E) a workforce partnership under subsection (d)(4)(N)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 2015(o)(1) another kind of program` THEN JUST FALSE

§ `Section 2015(o)(2): the work requirement`

-- ONE MONTH of the preceding 36-month period, as the person could state it.
DECLARE `s 2015(o)(2) month` HAS
    `the individual received benefits in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours worked per week, averaged monthly, in the month` IS A NUMBER
    `hours per week in a work program in the month, as determined by the State agency` IS A NUMBER
    `the individual complied with the requirements of the work program in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual participated in and complied with a program under section 2029 or a comparable program in the month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the individual received benefits in the month pursuant to paragraph (3), (4), (5), or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:788 | Subject to the other provisions of this subsection, no individual shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of any household if, during the preceding 36-month period, the individual received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for not less than 3 months (consecutive or otherwise) during which the individual did not—
-- src:789 | (A) work 20 hours or more per week, averaged monthly;
-- src:790 | (B) participate in and comply with the requirements of a work program for 20 hours or more per week, as determined by the State agency;
-- src:791 | (C) participate in and comply with the requirements of a program under section 2029 of this title or a comparable program established by a State or political subdivision of a State; or
-- src:792 | (D) receive benefits pursuant to paragraph (3), (4), (5), or (6).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(2) (src:788-792)
GIVEN m IS A `s 2015(o)(2) month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(2) the month is a benefit month in which the individual did none of the four things` MEANS
        m's `the individual received benefits in the month`
    AND (NOT (m's `hours worked per week, averaged monthly, in the month` AT LEAST 20))
    AND (NOT (m's `hours per week in a work program in the month, as determined by the State agency` AT LEAST 20 AND m's `the individual complied with the requirements of the work program in the month`))
    AND (NOT m's `the individual participated in and complied with a program under section 2029 or a comparable program in the month`)
    AND (NOT m's `the individual received benefits in the month pursuant to paragraph (3), (4), (5), or (6)`)

-- src:788 | Subject to the other provisions of this subsection, no individual shall be eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program as a member of any household if, during the preceding 36-month period, the individual received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for not less than 3 months (consecutive or otherwise) during which the individual did not—
-- src:789 | (A) work 20 hours or more per week, averaged monthly;
-- src:790 | (B) participate in and comply with the requirements of a work program for 20 hours or more per week, as determined by the State agency;
-- src:791 | (C) participate in and comply with the requirements of a program under section 2029 of this title or a comparable program established by a State or political subdivision of a State; or
-- src:792 | (D) receive benefits pursuant to paragraph (3), (4), (5), or (6).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(2) (src:788-792)
GIVEN `the months of the preceding 36-month period` IS A LIST OF `s 2015(o)(2) month`
      `an exception of paragraph (3) applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a waiver of paragraph (4) covers the area` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has regained eligibility under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a State exemption under paragraph (6) or (7) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(2) the individual is ineligible for failing the work requirement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence looks at "the preceding 36-month period", and a list of more than 36 months is not that period
        IF count `the months of the preceding 36-month period` GREATER THAN 36 THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to the other provisions of this subsection": a covering waiver, regained eligibility, or a State exemption
        IF `a waiver of paragraph (4) covers the area` OR `the individual has regained eligibility under paragraph (5)` OR `a State exemption under paragraph (6) or (7) applies` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) shall not apply to an individual if the individual is" within paragraph (3)
        IF `an exception of paragraph (3) applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        IF count (filter (GIVEN m YIELD `s 2015(o)(2) the month is a benefit month in which the individual did none of the four things` m) `the months of the preceding 36-month period`) AT LEAST 3 AND `an exception of paragraph (3) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): three or more such months, but whether paragraph (3) applies is not supplied
        IF count (filter (GIVEN m YIELD `s 2015(o)(2) the month is a benefit month in which the individual did none of the four things` m) `the months of the preceding 36-month period`) AT LEAST 3 THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, during the preceding 36-month period, the individual received supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits for not less than 3 months" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Section 2015(o)(3) to (5): exceptions, waiver, regaining eligibility`

-- src:794 | Paragraph (2) shall not apply to an individual if the individual is—
-- src:795 | (A) under 18, or over 65, years of age;
-- src:796 | (B) medically certified as physically or mentally unfit for employment;
-- src:797 | (C) a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for a dependent child under 14 years of age;
-- src:798 | (D) otherwise exempt under subsection (d)(2);
-- src:799 | (E) a pregnant woman;
-- src:800 | (F) an Indian or an Urban Indian (as such terms are defined in paragraphs (13) and (28) of section 1603 of title 25); or
-- src:801 | (G) a California Indian described in section 1679(a) of title 25.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(3) (src:794-801)
GIVEN person IS AN Individual
      `the individual is medically certified as physically or mentally unfit for employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of that child in years` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2015(d)(2) the person is exempt from the requirements of paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the individual is an Indian or an Urban Indian as defined in paragraphs (13) and (28) of section 1603 of title 25` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is a California Indian described in section 1679(a) of title 25` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(3) paragraph (2) does not apply to the individual` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (2) shall not apply to an individual if the individual is" (reading (a): none of items (A) to (G) is met)
    `s 2015 helper: some answer in the list holds`
        (LIST JUST (person's `age in years` LESS THAN 18 OR person's `age in years` GREATER THAN 65)
            , JUST `the individual is medically certified as physically or mentally unfit for employment`
            , JUST (`the individual is a parent or other member of a household with responsibility for a dependent child` AND `the age of that child in years` LESS THAN 14)
            , `s 2015(d)(2) the person is exempt from the requirements of paragraph (1)`
            , JUST (person's `pregnant`)
            , JUST `the individual is an Indian or an Urban Indian as defined in paragraphs (13) and (28) of section 1603 of title 25`
            , JUST `the individual is a California Indian described in section 1679(a) of title 25`)

-- src:803 | (A) In general
-- src:804 | On the request of a State agency and with the support of the chief executive officer of the State, the Secretary may waive the applicability of paragraph (2) to any group of individuals in the State if the Secretary makes a determination that the area in which the individuals reside—
-- src:805 | (i) has an unemployment rate of over 10 percent; or
-- src:806 | (ii) is in a noncontiguous State and has an unemployment rate that is at or above 1.5 times the national unemployment rate.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(4)(A) (src:803-806)
GIVEN `the State agency has requested the waiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the chief executive officer of the State supports the request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary has determined that the area in which the individuals reside qualifies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the unemployment rate of the area, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
      `the State in which the area lies` IS AN Area
      `the national unemployment rate, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(4)(A) the Secretary may waive the applicability of paragraph (2) to the group of individuals` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the request of a State agency and with the support of the chief executive officer of the State"
        IF NOT (`the State agency has requested the waiver` AND `the chief executive officer of the State supports the request`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary makes a determination that the area ... (i) has an unemployment rate of over 10 percent; or (ii) is in a noncontiguous State and has an unemployment rate that is at or above 1.5 times the national unemployment rate" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT (`the unemployment rate of the area, as a fraction` GREATER THAN 0.1 OR (`s 2015(o)(4)(C) the place is a noncontiguous State` `the State in which the area lies` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the unemployment rate of the area, as a fraction` AT LEAST 1.5 TIMES `the national unemployment rate, as a fraction`)) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary makes a determination that the area in which the individuals reside—" (reading (a): no determination, no waiver)
        IF `the Secretary has determined that the area in which the individuals reside qualifies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Secretary has made the determination is not supplied; and the waiver itself is the Secretary's choice ("may")
        OTHERWISE `the Secretary has determined that the area in which the individuals reside qualifies`

-- src:807 | (B) Report
-- src:808 | The Secretary shall report the basis for a waiver under subparagraph (A) to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(4)(B) (src:807-808)
GIVEN `the Secretary has granted a waiver under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(4)(B) the Secretary is required to report the basis for the waiver to the Committees` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary shall report the basis for a waiver under subparagraph (A) to the Committee on Agriculture of the House of Representatives and the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry of the Senate"
    IF `the Secretary has granted a waiver under subparagraph (A)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:809 | (C) Definition of noncontiguous State
-- src:810 | (i) In general
-- src:811 | In this paragraph, the term “noncontiguous State” means a State that is not 1 of the contiguous 48 States or the District of Columbia.
-- src:812 | (ii) Exclusions
-- src:813 | The term “noncontiguous State” does not include Guam or the Virgin Islands of the United States.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(4)(C) (src:809-813)
GIVEN place IS AN Area
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(4)(C) the place is a noncontiguous State` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“noncontiguous State” means a State that is not 1 of the contiguous 48 States or the District of Columbia", so the 48 States and the District are not; and "does not include Guam or the Virgin Islands of the United States"
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `Alaska, urban` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Alaska, rural 1` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Alaska, rural 2` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN Guam THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN Hawaii THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the Virgin Islands of the United States` THEN JUST FALSE

-- src:815 | (A) Regaining eligibility
-- src:816 | An individual denied eligibility under paragraph (2) shall regain eligibility to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if, during a 30-day period, the individual—
-- src:817 | (i) works 80 or more hours;
-- src:818 | (ii) participates in and complies with the requirements of a work program for 80 or more hours, as determined by a State agency; or
-- src:819 | (iii) participates in and complies with the requirements of a program under section 2029 of this title or a comparable program established by a State or political subdivision of a State.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(5)(A) (src:815-819)
GIVEN `the individual was denied eligibility under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hours the individual worked in the 30-day period` IS A NUMBER
      `hours the individual participated in a work program in the 30-day period, as determined by a State agency` IS A NUMBER
      `the individual complied with the requirements of the work program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual participated in and complied with a program under section 2029 or a comparable program in the 30-day period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(5)(A) the individual regains eligibility` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An individual denied eligibility under paragraph (2)"
        IF NOT `the individual was denied eligibility under paragraph (2)` THEN NOTHING
        IF `hours the individual worked in the 30-day period` AT LEAST 80
           OR (`hours the individual participated in a work program in the 30-day period, as determined by a State agency` AT LEAST 80 AND `the individual complied with the requirements of the work program`)
           OR `the individual participated in and complied with a program under section 2029 or a comparable program in the 30-day period`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall regain eligibility ... if, during a 30-day period, the individual— (i) works 80 or more hours; (ii) ...; or (iii) ..." (reading (a): a failed "if")
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:820 | (B) Maintaining eligibility
-- src:821 | An individual who regains eligibility under subparagraph (A) shall remain eligible as long as the individual meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(5)(B) (src:820-821)
GIVEN `the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(5)(B) the individual remains eligible` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An individual who regains eligibility under subparagraph (A)"
        IF NOT `the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall remain eligible as long as the individual meets the requirements"
        IF NOT `the individual meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:823 | (i) In general
-- src:824 | An individual who regained eligibility under subparagraph (A) and who no longer meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2) shall remain eligible for a consecutive 3-month period, beginning on the date the individual first notifies the State agency that the individual no longer meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2).
-- src:825 | (ii) Limitation
-- src:826 | An individual shall not receive any benefits pursuant to clause (i) for more than a single 3-month period in any 36-month period.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(5)(C) (src:823-826)
GIVEN `the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual no longer meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the individual first notified the State agency` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the individual received benefits pursuant to clause (i) for a 3-month period within the 36 months before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(5)(C) the individual remains eligible on the date for the 3-month period` MEANS
    -- MONTH ARITHMETIC (fork F-mo, NOTES): "a consecutive 3-month period, beginning on the date the individual first notifies" is computed with `add months`, which CLAMPS the day to the last day of a shorter month (31 January 2026 plus 1 month is 28 February 2026). The text does not say how a month is counted when the later month lacks the day; the other readings are "not covered" and rolling forward.
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An individual who regained eligibility under subparagraph (A) and who no longer meets the requirements"
        IF NOT (`the individual regained eligibility under subparagraph (A)` AND `the individual no longer meets the requirements of subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)`) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not receive any benefits pursuant to clause (i) for more than a single 3-month period in any 36-month period"
        IF `the individual received benefits pursuant to clause (i) for a 3-month period within the 36 months before` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a date before the notification is not within the period that begins "on the date the individual first notifies the State agency"
        IF `the date asked about` LESS THAN `the date the individual first notified the State agency` THEN NOTHING
        -- fork F-o3: a 3-month period that begins on the 15th of January ends on the 14th of April, as `add months` counts it; the other reading would include the 15th of April
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a consecutive 3-month period, beginning on the date the individual first notifies the State agency"
        IF `the date asked about` AT LEAST `add months` `the date the individual first notified the State agency` 3 THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 2015(o)(6): exemptions the State agency may give`

-- src:830 | (i) Caseload
-- src:831 | The term “caseload” means the average monthly number of individuals receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the 12-month period ending the preceding June 30.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(A)(i) (src:830-831)
GIVEN `the average monthly numbers of individuals receiving benefits in the 12 months ending the preceding June 30` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2015(o)(6)(A)(i) the caseload` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the average monthly number of individuals receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the 12-month period ending the preceding June 30"; fewer or more than 12 monthly numbers is not that period
    IF count `the average monthly numbers of individuals receiving benefits in the 12 months ending the preceding June 30` EQUALS 12
        THEN JUST (sum `the average monthly numbers of individuals receiving benefits in the 12 months ending the preceding June 30` DIVIDED BY 12)
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:832 | (ii) Covered individual
-- src:833 | The term “covered individual” means a member of a household that receives supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits, or an individual denied eligibility for supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits solely due to paragraph (2), who—
-- src:834 | (I) is not eligible for an exception under paragraph (3);
-- src:835 | (II) does not reside in an area covered by a waiver granted under paragraph (4);
-- src:836 | (III) is not complying with subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2);
-- src:837 | (IV) is not receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits during the 3 months of eligibility provided under paragraph (2); and
-- src:838 | (V) is not receiving supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits under paragraph (5).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(A)(ii) (src:832-838)
GIVEN `the individual is a member of a household that receives benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual was denied eligibility solely due to paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is not eligible for an exception under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual does not reside in an area covered by a waiver granted under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is not complying with subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is not receiving benefits during the 3 months of eligibility provided under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is not receiving benefits under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(6)(A)(ii) the individual is a covered individual` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “covered individual” means a member of a household that receives ... benefits, or an individual denied eligibility ... solely due to paragraph (2), who— (I) ...; (II) ...; (III) ...; (IV) ...; and (V) ..."
    JUST ((`the individual is a member of a household that receives benefits` OR `the individual was denied eligibility solely due to paragraph (2)`)
          AND `the individual is not eligible for an exception under paragraph (3)`
          AND `the individual does not reside in an area covered by a waiver granted under paragraph (4)`
          AND `the individual is not complying with subparagraph (A), (B), or (C) of paragraph (2)`
          AND `the individual is not receiving benefits during the 3 months of eligibility provided under paragraph (2)`
          AND `the individual is not receiving benefits under paragraph (5)`)

-- src:839 | (B) General rule
-- src:840 | Subject to subparagraphs (C) through (I), a State agency may provide an exemption from the requirements of paragraph (2) for covered individuals.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(B) (src:839-840)
GIVEN `the individual is a covered individual` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the average monthly number of exemptions is within the limit of subparagraphs (C) through (I)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(6)(B) the State agency may provide an exemption from paragraph (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual is a covered individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the average monthly number of exemptions is within the limit of subparagraphs (C) through (I)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subparagraphs (C) through (I), a State agency may provide an exemption" (reading (a): beyond the limit of (C) to (F) the permission does not reach)
        IF `the individual is a covered individual` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the average monthly number of exemptions is within the limit of subparagraphs (C) through (I)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may provide an exemption from the requirements of paragraph (2) for covered individuals": the text speaks only of covered individuals
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:841 | (C) Fiscal year 1998
-- src:842 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) and (I), for fiscal year 1998, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of the exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 15 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State in fiscal year 1998, as estimated by the Secretary, based on the survey conducted to carry out section 2025(c) of this title for fiscal year 1996 and such other factors as the Secretary considers appropriate due to the timing and limitations of the survey.
-- src:843 | (D) Fiscal years 1999 through 2019
-- src:844 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) through (I), for fiscal year 1999 and each subsequent fiscal year through fiscal year 2019, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of the exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 15 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State, as estimated by the Secretary under subparagraph (C), adjusted by the Secretary to reflect changes in the State’s caseload and the Secretary’s estimate of changes in the proportion of members of households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits covered by waivers granted under paragraph (4).
-- src:845 | (E) Fiscal years 2020 through 2023
-- src:846 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) through (I), for fiscal year 2020 and each subsequent fiscal year through fiscal year 2023, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 12 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State, as estimated by the Secretary under subparagraph (C), adjusted by the Secretary to reflect changes in the State’s caseload and the Secretary’s estimate of changes in the proportion of members of households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits covered by waivers granted under paragraph (4).
-- src:847 | (F) Subsequent fiscal years
-- src:848 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) through (I), for fiscal years 2024 and each subsequent fiscal year, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 8 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State, as estimated by the Secretary under subparagraph (C), adjusted by the Secretary to reflect changes in the State’s caseload and the Secretary’s estimate of changes in the proportion of members of households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits covered by waivers granted under paragraph (4) [Footnote: 1 So in original. Probably should be followed by a period.]
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(C) to (F) (src:841-848)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2015(o)(6)(C) to (F) the percentage of covered individuals for the fiscal year` MEANS
    -- UNIT: the result is a FRACTION, not the printed percent (15 percent is 0.15), as in the header of this module; a caller holding "15 percent" passes or expects 0.15.
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no fiscal year before 1998 is named
        IF `the fiscal year` LESS THAN 1998 THEN NOTHING
        -- (C) "for fiscal year 1998 ... does not exceed 15 percent" and (D) "fiscal year 1999 and each subsequent fiscal year through fiscal year 2019"
        IF `the fiscal year` AT MOST 2019 THEN JUST 0.15
        -- (E) "fiscal year 2020 and each subsequent fiscal year through fiscal year 2023 ... does not exceed 12 percent"
        IF `the fiscal year` AT MOST 2023 THEN JUST 0.12
        -- (F) "for fiscal years 2024 and each subsequent fiscal year ... does not exceed 8 percent"
        OTHERWISE JUST 0.08

-- src:841 | (C) Fiscal year 1998
-- src:842 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) and (I), for fiscal year 1998, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of the exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 15 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State in fiscal year 1998, as estimated by the Secretary, based on the survey conducted to carry out section 2025(c) of this title for fiscal year 1996 and such other factors as the Secretary considers appropriate due to the timing and limitations of the survey.
-- src:843 | (D) Fiscal years 1999 through 2019
-- src:844 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) through (I), for fiscal year 1999 and each subsequent fiscal year through fiscal year 2019, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of the exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 15 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State, as estimated by the Secretary under subparagraph (C), adjusted by the Secretary to reflect changes in the State’s caseload and the Secretary’s estimate of changes in the proportion of members of households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits covered by waivers granted under paragraph (4).
-- src:845 | (E) Fiscal years 2020 through 2023
-- src:846 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) through (I), for fiscal year 2020 and each subsequent fiscal year through fiscal year 2023, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 12 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State, as estimated by the Secretary under subparagraph (C), adjusted by the Secretary to reflect changes in the State’s caseload and the Secretary’s estimate of changes in the proportion of members of households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits covered by waivers granted under paragraph (4).
-- src:847 | (F) Subsequent fiscal years
-- src:848 | Subject to subparagraphs (G) through (I), for fiscal years 2024 and each subsequent fiscal year, a State agency may provide a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed 8 percent of the number of covered individuals in the State, as estimated by the Secretary under subparagraph (C), adjusted by the Secretary to reflect changes in the State’s caseload and the Secretary’s estimate of changes in the proportion of members of households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits covered by waivers granted under paragraph (4) [Footnote: 1 So in original. Probably should be followed by a period.]
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(C) to (F) (src:841-848)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary's estimate of the number of covered individuals in the State, as adjusted` IS A NUMBER
      `the average monthly number of exemptions in effect during the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(6)(C) to (F) the average monthly number of exemptions in effect is within the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2015(o)(6)(C) to (F) the percentage of covered individuals for the fiscal year` `the fiscal year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a number of exemptions such that the average monthly number of the exemptions in effect during the fiscal year does not exceed" the percentage of covered individuals
        IF `the average monthly number of exemptions in effect during the fiscal year` GREATER THAN p TIMES `the Secretary's estimate of the number of covered individuals in the State, as adjusted` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:849 | (G) Caseload adjustments
-- src:850 | The Secretary shall adjust the number of individuals estimated for a State under subparagraph (C), (D),, [Footnote: 2 So in original.] (E) or (F) during a fiscal year if the number of members of households that receive supplemental nutrition assistance program benefits in the State varies from the State’s caseload by more than 10 percent, as determined by the Secretary.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(G) (src:849-850)
GIVEN `the number of members of households receiving benefits in the State` IS A NUMBER
      `the State's caseload` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(6)(G) the Secretary is required to adjust the number of individuals estimated for the State` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall adjust ... if the number of members of households that receive ... benefits in the State varies from the State’s caseload by more than 10 percent" (reading (a): a failed "if"; exactly 10 percent is not more than 10 percent)
    IF `the number of members of households receiving benefits in the State` GREATER THAN `the State's caseload` TIMES 1.1 OR `the number of members of households receiving benefits in the State` LESS THAN `the State's caseload` TIMES 0.9 THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:851 | (H) Exemption adjustments
-- src:852 | During fiscal year 1999 and each subsequent fiscal year, the Secretary shall increase or decrease the number of individuals who may be granted an exemption by a State agency under this paragraph to the extent that the average monthly number of exemptions in effect in the State for the preceding fiscal year under this paragraph is lesser or greater than the average monthly number of exemptions estimated for the State agency for such preceding fiscal year under this paragraph.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(H) (src:851-852)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the average monthly number of exemptions in effect in the State for the preceding fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the average monthly number of exemptions estimated for the State agency for the preceding fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2015(o)(6)(H) the increase or decrease in the number of individuals who may be granted an exemption` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "During fiscal year 1999 and each subsequent fiscal year"
    -- a positive number is an increase and a negative number a decrease: "to the extent that the average monthly number of exemptions in effect ... for the preceding fiscal year is lesser or greater than the average monthly number of exemptions estimated"
    IF `the fiscal year` LESS THAN 1999 THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the average monthly number of exemptions estimated for the State agency for the preceding fiscal year` MINUS `the average monthly number of exemptions in effect in the State for the preceding fiscal year`)

-- src:853 | (I) Reporting requirement
-- src:854 | A State agency shall submit such reports to the Secretary as the Secretary determines are necessary to ensure compliance with this paragraph.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(I) (src:853-854)
GIVEN `the Secretary has determined that the report is necessary to ensure compliance with this paragraph` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(6)(I) the State agency is required to submit the report to the Secretary` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "A State agency shall submit such reports to the Secretary as the Secretary determines are necessary to ensure compliance with this paragraph"
    IF `the Secretary has determined that the report is necessary to ensure compliance with this paragraph` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:855 | (J) Rule of construction for exemption adjustment
-- src:856 | During fiscal year 2024 and each subsequent fiscal year, nothing in this paragraph shall be interpreted to allow a State agency to accumulate unused exemptions to be provided beyond the subsequent fiscal year.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(6)(J) (src:855-856)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the exemptions would be provided beyond the subsequent fiscal year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(6)(J) the State agency may accumulate unused exemptions to be provided beyond the subsequent fiscal year` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this paragraph shall be interpreted to allow a State agency to accumulate unused exemptions to be provided beyond the subsequent fiscal year"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "During fiscal year 2024 and each subsequent fiscal year"
    IF `the fiscal year` AT LEAST 2024 AND `the exemptions would be provided beyond the subsequent fiscal year` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 2015(o)(7) and (8): noncontiguous States, and other program rules`

-- src:858 | (A) Definition of noncontiguous State
-- src:859 | (i) In general
-- src:860 | In this paragraph, the term “noncontiguous State” means a State that is not 1 of the contiguous 48 States or the District of Columbia.
-- src:861 | (ii) Exclusions
-- src:862 | In this paragraph, the term “noncontiguous State” does not include Guam or the Virgin Islands of the United States.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(7)(A) (src:858-862)
GIVEN place IS AN Area
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(7)(A) the place is a noncontiguous State` MEANS
    -- the definition is repeated word for word from paragraph (4)(C); the answer is the same
    `s 2015(o)(4)(C) the place is a noncontiguous State` place

-- src:864 | Subject to subparagraph (D), the Secretary may exempt individuals in a noncontiguous State from compliance with the requirements of paragraph (2) if—
-- src:865 | (i) the State agency submits to the Secretary a request for that exemption, made in such form and at such time as the Secretary may require, and including the information described in subparagraph (C); and
-- src:866 | (ii) the Secretary determines that based on that request, the State agency is demonstrating a good faith effort to comply with the requirements of paragraph (2).
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(7)(B) (src:864-866)
GIVEN `s 2015(o)(7)(A) the State is a noncontiguous State` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State agency submitted a request in the form and at the time the Secretary requires, with the information described in subparagraph (C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that, based on the request, the State agency is demonstrating a good faith effort to comply with paragraph (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(7)(B) the Secretary may exempt individuals in the noncontiguous State from paragraph (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Secretary may exempt individuals in a noncontiguous State"
        IF NOT (`s 2015(o)(7)(A) the State is a noncontiguous State` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if— (i) the State agency submits to the Secretary a request for that exemption" (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF NOT `the State agency submitted a request in the form and at the time the Secretary requires, with the information described in subparagraph (C)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- (ii) "the Secretary determines that based on that request, the State agency is demonstrating a good faith effort": the determination is an input
        OTHERWISE `the Secretary determines that, based on the request, the State agency is demonstrating a good faith effort to comply with paragraph (2)`

-- src:867 | (C) Good faith effort determination
-- src:868 | In determining whether a State agency is demonstrating a good faith effort for purposes of subparagraph (B)(ii), the Secretary shall consider—
-- src:869 | (i) any actions taken by the State agency toward compliance with the requirements of paragraph (2);
-- src:870 | (ii) any significant barriers to or challenges in meeting those requirements, including barriers or challenges relating to funding, design, development, procurement, or installation of necessary systems or resources;
-- src:871 | (iii) the detailed plan and timeline of the State agency for achieving full compliance with those requirements, including any milestones (as defined by the Secretary); and
-- src:872 | (iv) any other criteria determined appropriate by the Secretary.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(7)(C) (src:867-872)
GIVEN `the matter is one of items (i) to (iv): the State agency's actions, its barriers or challenges, its plan and timeline, or other criteria the Secretary finds appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(7)(C) the Secretary is required to consider the matter in determining good faith effort` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Secretary shall consider— (i) any actions taken ...; (ii) any significant barriers ...; (iii) the detailed plan and timeline ...; and (iv) any other criteria determined appropriate by the Secretary"
    IF `the matter is one of items (i) to (iv): the State agency's actions, its barriers or challenges, its plan and timeline, or other criteria the Secretary finds appropriate` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:874 | (i) In general
-- src:875 | An exemption granted under subparagraph (B) shall expire not later than December 31, 2028, and may not be renewed beyond that date.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(7)(D)(i) (src:874-875)
GIVEN `the date the exemption would expire` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(7)(D)(i) the exemption may run until the date` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall expire not later than December 31, 2028, and may not be renewed beyond that date"
    IF `the date the exemption would expire` AT MOST (Date 31 12 2028) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:876 | (ii) Early termination
-- src:877 | The Secretary may terminate an exemption granted under subparagraph (B) prior to the expiration date of that exemption if the Secretary determines that the State agency—
-- src:878 | (I) has failed to comply with the reporting requirements described in subparagraph (E); or
-- src:879 | (II) based on the information provided pursuant to subparagraph (E), failed to make continued good faith efforts toward compliance with the requirements of this subsection.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(7)(D)(ii) (src:876-879)
GIVEN `the date asked about is before the expiration date of the exemption` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that the State agency failed to comply with the reporting requirements of subparagraph (E)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that, based on the information provided under subparagraph (E), the State agency failed to make continued good faith efforts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(7)(D)(ii) the Secretary may terminate the exemption early` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may terminate an exemption ... prior to the expiration date"
        IF NOT `the date asked about is before the expiration date of the exemption` THEN NOTHING
        IF `s 2015 helper: at least one answer holds` `the Secretary determines that the State agency failed to comply with the reporting requirements of subparagraph (E)` `the Secretary determines that, based on the information provided under subparagraph (E), the State agency failed to make continued good faith efforts` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the Secretary determines that the State agency— (I) ...; or (II) ..." (reading (a): a failed "if")
        IF `s 2015 helper: at least one answer holds` `the Secretary determines that the State agency failed to comply with the reporting requirements of subparagraph (E)` `the Secretary determines that, based on the information provided under subparagraph (E), the State agency failed to make continued good faith efforts` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:880 | (E) Reporting requirements
-- src:881 | A State agency granted an exemption under subparagraph (B) shall submit to the Secretary—
-- src:882 | (i) quarterly progress reports on the status of the State agency in achieving the milestones toward full compliance described in subparagraph (C)(iii); and
-- src:883 | (ii) information on specific risks or newly identified barriers or challenges to full compliance, including the plan of the State agency to mitigate those risks, barriers, or challenges.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(7)(E) (src:880-883)
GIVEN `the State agency was granted an exemption under subparagraph (B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(7)(E) the State agency is required to submit the quarterly progress reports and the information on risks and barriers` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A State agency granted an exemption under subparagraph (B)"
    IF `the State agency was granted an exemption under subparagraph (B)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:884 | (8) Other program rules
-- src:885 | Nothing in this subsection shall make an individual eligible for benefits under this chapter if the individual is not otherwise eligible for benefits under the other provisions of this chapter.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2015(o)(8) (src:884-885)
GIVEN `the individual is otherwise eligible for benefits under the other provisions of this chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2015(o)(8) this subsection makes the individual eligible for benefits` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this subsection shall make an individual eligible for benefits under this chapter if the individual is not otherwise eligible"
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): an individual who is otherwise eligible, or whose eligibility is not supplied
    IF `the individual is otherwise eligible for benefits under the other provisions of this chapter` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
